    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x559876571ce0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">give malachite to first ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The ghost takes the malachite and looks at it inquisitively. He holds it close. You can see his emotional barriers breaking down. He looks at you and very slowly starts to smile. &quot;I... I see now that I had no choice. I was a victim as much as they were. If I had not killed them I would have been killed myself. I see a long road ahead...&quot; He looks at you, a single tear rolling down his cheek as he smiles, the relief obvious in his face. &quot;But... I think I am beginning to forgive myself.&quot;

The ghost slowly begins to dissolve and rise upwards into the desert sky. Where he stood, an ornate tombstone with a roman numeral carved into it rests on the ground.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x5598765752b0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x5598765752b0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">whisper sarruma</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The feather seems to glow dimly. Suddenly you are enveloped in ethereal light so bright that you are forced to close your eyes. When the light fades and you open your eyes again, you are elsewhere...

Mountain Overlook
You stand on the slope of a tall mountain. A sheer drop falls away to the southwest. Torrential rain hammers down all around you, leaving the stone floor dangerously slippery and soaking you to the bone. You can see the entrance to a cavern to the northeast,but the downpour has caused the mountain stream to expand into a hazardous deluge which is impossible to cross.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x5598765785c0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x5598765785c0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">ne</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The stream has become a overflowing cascade.  Stepping into that would surely sweep you over the edge of the cliff. You briefly contemplate how long it would take you to fall to the bottom and decide you do not wish to find out.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x55987657b940"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x55987657b940">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at the stream</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A rushing torrent of water cascades across the floor between you and the cavern entrance and flows with great force over the edge of the cliff.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x55987657eeb0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x55987657eeb0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">yell bollocks</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You yell &quot;BOLLOCKS!&quot; It feels somewhat cathartic, but ultimately futile.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x559876582470"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x559876582470">
    <command xml:space="preserve">yell STOP RAINING</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You yell at the clouds, at the sky, at the very gods themselves, and miraculously (or coincidentally, depending on your viewpoint), they seem to listen. The rain eases, then stops. The clouds begin to break, revealing a beautiful fiery orange sunset to the southwest. Gradually, the mountain stream reduces in ferocity. The air feels incredibly still and you are overcome with a sense of tranquility.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x559876585820"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x559876585820">
    <command xml:space="preserve">yell stop raining</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The rain has stopped; the mountains are peaceful. You see no reason to change that.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x559876588e10"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x559876588e10">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Mountain Overlook
You stand on the slope of a tall mountain. A sheer drop falls away to the southwest.  You can see the entrance to a cavern to the northeast, on the other side of a shallow mountain stream.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>YES</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
